{
  "body" : "You are designing a minimalist studio portrait with a clean aesthetic and reflective surfaces.\n\nCONTENT BRIEF\n- Primary subject: {{subject}}\n- Backdrop atmosphere: {{setting}}\n- On-image text: {{copy}}\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\n- Genre / medium: editorial studio photography\n- Composition: centered subject, tall aspect ratio (3:2 portrait), balanced use of negative space with focus on the subject's posture and expression\n- Lens / camera: medium focal length (~50mm), sharp focus with subtle depth of field to isolate the subject\n- Lighting: soft and even lighting, high-key white illumination from behind, subtle shadows to define form\n- Color palette and grading: monochromatic with emphasis on black and white tones; muted highlights and deep shadows\n- Texture / surface: smooth and polished surfaces, reflective floor creating subtle mirror effects\n- Post-processing: clean and precise editing, no visible grain, soft transitions in gradients\n- Mood: elegant, introspective, modern\n- References: Petra Collins studio minimalism, Vogue editorial lighting, high-fashion reflective compositions\n\nDESIGN RULES\n- Aspect: 3:2 portrait (~1024×1536), suitable for editorial layouts and vertical presentation\n- Ensure the subject is centered and occupies approximately two-thirds of the frame, with ample negative space around\n- Maintain clean lines and reflective surfaces without visual distractions\n\nAVOID\n- Harsh shadows or direct on-camera flash\n- Busy or cluttered environments\n- Over-saturation or vibrant color palettes\n- Distracting props or accessories that overwhelm the minimal aesthetic\n- Visible digital artifacts or chromatic aberration\n\nAdditional constraints: {{extra}}\n\n——————\nSubject: {{subject}}\nSetting: {{setting}}\nCopy: {{copy}}\nExtra notes: {{extra}}",
